 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Venice is a whole city built on water. So what is it standing on?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Millions of wooden logs, hammered straight down into the mud.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But wood in the ground should rot in a few years. Just look at an old fence post.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Rot is fungus eating the wood, and fungus needs air to live.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The Venice logs are always underwater, packed in mud, where there's almost no oxygen.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So the fungus can't grow, and the wood soaks up minerals and turns hard.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Some of those logs have been down there for many centuries.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "One church alone, Santa Maria della Salute, stands on about a million of them.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Keep wood away from air, and it can last almost forever. Now you know.",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
